    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1460">

                <pb facs="1180" n="1064" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1064"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 817.00/2159.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Consul at Bluefields to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 86.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Bluefields, Nicaragua</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-11-09">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 9, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to confirm the following
                    telegram to the Department, which was sent on October 16th by wireless via
                    Colón: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>I have to suggest that the <hi rendition="#italic">Tacoma</hi> be
                            withdrawn, as there is no danger of any trouble now, all being quiet
                            here.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Thinking that the ship may be needed elsewhere, and as it appeared to me that all
                    danger had passed, I sent the above telegram. The ship received instructions on
                    October 19th to proceed to Tampico, Mexico.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.],</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Arthur J. Clare.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
